I've got Nethack 2.3e running on 4.3BSD Unix, which is running on a
SIMH-simulated VAX-11/780.

4.3BSD was released in June 1986.  It won't run on modern hardware,
but you can run the SIMH simulator under Windows or Linux to simulate
the old VAX hardware that it runs on.

Nethack 2.3e compiles and runs fine on this platform.  Just need to
copy "Makefile.unix" to "Makefile" and run "make".


